* **Attack 6 — Q4 Candidate (2): Confirming `csr3 mix`'s HEAD want `0x0015` against Section 3 (`SEC1:17-18`, `SEC3:6-10`, `L0_TABLE:11`, `SEC5:33-34`).**
  * **Status:** **HOLDS** (`READ` and `DERIVED` from `L0_TABLE:11`, `SEC3:6-10`, `DIFF:16`).
  * **Analysis:** In `L0_TABLE:11` (`READ`), the row is:
    `csr3 mix     0x0015     head 0x0015   fix 0x0005   [FIX] FAIL`
    On the pre-fix binary (`base`), `got` is `0x0015`, which equals `head 0x0015` (confirming the HEAD column leg passed `20/20` at `SEC3:6`, `READ`) and differs from `fix 0x0005` (producing one of the three `[FIX] FAIL` rows in L0's `17/20` at `SEC3:7` and `L0_TABLE:23`, `READ`). Arithmetically, under H1 (`d->reg[r] = x & 0x0007;` at `DIFF:16` / `CODE:50`), writing `0x0015` stores `0x0015 & 0x0007 == 0x0005` (`DERIVED`), which matches `fix 0x0005` and passes `20/20` on L1 and L2 (`SEC3:9-10`, `READ`).

